# Scoped to the front end rather than added to the repo-root .gitignore: the
# root file is about the Python project, and a Node toolchain's ignore rules
# belong next to the Node toolchain. It also means `web/` can be lifted out
# wholesale without losing them.
#
# node_modules is ~250 MB for this one page. The root .gitignore does not
# mention it -- there was no Node code in the repo until now -- so without this
# a `git add web/` stages 2,186 dependency files.
node_modules/

# Build output. Already matched by the root .gitignore's bare `dist/`, repeated
# here so this directory is self-describing.
dist/
